# [MoE] Add fused_moe(stage2_fp8=True): per-call FP8 stage-2 route output
# https://github.com/ROCm/aiter/pull/8174  (PR head 286cda38b8, on AITER main 1f1e0ec525)
# Generated against the 20261117 image's AITER checkout (581579ab5); source files only (tests dropped).
# fused_moe(stage2_fp8=True) makes one call's FlyDSL layout reduce stage 2 write FP8 route rows summed in fp32 (what
# AITER_FLYDSL_STAGE2_FP8=1 does for every call); after an MXMOE stage 1, an MXFP4 scatter stage 2 with bf16 output runs
# as the reduce stage 2 of the same tile. Without the argument every call is unchanged. Patch 23 passes it.
# Port onto 581579ab5 (the PR builds on aiter#7135 and other main commits 581579ab5 lacks): the PR's hunks re-anchored;
# two have no counterpart and are left out: the deterministic=True refusal (581579ab5's fused_moe takes no
# deterministic argument) and main's AITER_MXFP4_INTERMEDIATE term in fused_moe_2stages' route-weight condition.
# Apply in /sgl-workspace/aiter with git apply.

